# S9 — metadata-similarity-assembly (QM), census docs/PICT_CENSUS.md § S9.
# See tests/models/metadata-similarity-assembly.oracle.ts for the oracle spec.
#
# `findBestBankMetadataForSlot` (assessmentVariantService.js:404) picks the
# best-scoring bank question via `scoreMetadataMatch`
# (assessmentVariantMetadataScoring.js): topic +100 / type +50 / difficulty
# +25 / reasoning +10, against a 75 cutoff (`MIN_METADATA_SCORE`, :399).
# `HasFallback` is deliberately constrained to only matter when `AlreadyUsed`
# is "yes": a fallback candidate coexisting with an available primary would
# just make the "which one wins" comparison ambiguous on a score tie without
# adding real model value, so this model keeps the fallback scoped to its
# actual purpose — rescuing a slot when the best candidate was already
# consumed by an earlier slot in the same exam.
TopicMatch:      yes, no
TypeMatch:       yes, no
DifficultyMatch: yes, no
ReasoningMatch:  yes, no
AlreadyUsed:     yes, no
HasFallback:     yes, no

IF [AlreadyUsed] = "no" THEN [HasFallback] = "no";
